--
C++20 std::iterator_traits<__normal_iterator<...>>::iterator_category, end to end.

The underlying root cause -- selecting the constrained __iterator_traits partial
specialization by its requires-clause ([temp.class.spec.match]/[temp.constr.order])
-- is now fixed (see cpp20_constrained_partial_spec), so
iterator_traits<...>::iterator_category resolves to random_access_iterator_tag.

This end-to-end case via std::vector<int>::iterator remains KNOWNBUG: resolving
the category now lets the full std::vector instantiation proceed, which hits a
further (separate) front-end instantiation throw that truncates main, so the
assertion is not yet reached.  That is the next cluster-#1 layer.

The minimal, genuine regression for the constrained-partial-specialization fix
is cpp20_constrained_partial_spec (CORE).  Reclassify this end-to-end case CORE
once the remaining std::vector-iterator instantiation issue is resolved.
